 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n### Issue with JSON Extraction Functions in BigQuery Dialect\n\n#### Describe the Bug\n\nIt seems there's an issue with the JSON extraction functions in the BigQuery dialect. When attempting to use JSON extraction functions like `JSON_QUERY`, `JSON_VALUE`, or `JSON_QUERY_ARRAY`, the generated SQL does not behave as expected. This issue arises when handling optional arguments such as `ON ERROR`, `ON EMPTY`, and `RETURNING`.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\nHere's a simplified example to illustrate the problem:\n\n```python\nfrom sqlglot import parse_one\nfrom sqlglot.dialects import BigQuery\n\n# Example JSON extraction\nsql = \"SELECT JSON_QUERY(data, '$.path') FROM my_table\"\nexpression = parse_one(sql, read='bigquery')\n\n# Attempt to generate SQL\ngenerator = BigQuery.Generator()\ngenerated_sql = generator.sql(expression)\nprint(generated_sql)\n```\n\n#### Expected Results\n\nThe SQL should be generated correctly with the appropriate JSON extraction function and optional clauses.\n\n#### Actual Results\n\nThe generated SQL does not include the expected JSON extraction function or handles optional clauses incorrectly, leading to unexpected behavior.\n\n#### Additional Information\n\nThis issue affects the handling of JSON extraction functions in the BigQuery dialect, particularly when optional arguments are involved. It may also impact other dialects that rely on similar JSON extraction logic.\n</issue>\n",
